// Copy to `Secrets.xcconfig` (gitignored) and fill in the token. The Xcode
// project references Secrets.xcconfig as its base configuration and injects
// SCAN_API_TOKEN into the app's Info.plist as `ScanAPIToken`, which
// ScanAPIConfig reads at runtime. Nothing secret ever enters the repo.
//
// CI creates Secrets.xcconfig from a GitHub Actions secret before building; a
// missing file only warns (the app then reports "Scanning isn't set up").
//
// Value: the worker's SCAN_API_TOKEN secret. NOTE — xcconfig treats `//` as a
// comment, so if `openssl rand -base64 32` ever yields a token containing `//`,
// regenerate it.
SCAN_API_TOKEN = your-scan-api-token
